WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.384 --> 00:00:04.217
- Um...

00:00:04.217 --> 00:00:05.368
(laughing)

00:00:05.368 --> 00:00:07.100
(upbeat jazz music

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.384
- I love dark chocolate.

00:00:09.384 --> 00:00:10.747
Chocolate makes me happy, man.

00:00:10.747 --> 00:00:12.824
It gets me through some stressful days.

00:00:12.824 --> 00:00:15.120
It's sweet. It just brings joy to my life.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.741
What's there not to like about chocolate?

00:00:16.741 --> 00:00:18.908
- Just thinking about chocolate
is making my mouth water

00:00:18.908 --> 00:00:20.257
and it's making my heart happy

00:00:20.257 --> 00:00:22.961
because chocolate has
always been a reward.

00:00:22.961 --> 00:00:24.467
It's always been an indulgence.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:27.135
Chocolate is the purest joy in the world

00:00:27.135 --> 00:00:28.992
next to dogs and cats.

00:00:28.992 --> 00:00:31.605
- I think 100% dark chocolate is gonna be

00:00:31.605 --> 00:00:34.499
mind-blowingly amazing, super sweet.

00:00:34.499 --> 00:00:36.315
Pure dark chocolate,
it's gonna be the best.

00:00:36.315 --> 00:00:37.690
- Yeah.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.304
So we are here at Tache

00:00:39.304 --> 00:00:42.109
in the Lower East Side of New York City,

00:00:42.109 --> 00:00:45.461
and we are going to
learn all about chocolate

00:00:45.461 --> 00:00:49.510
and eventually try 100% pure chocolate.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:51.703
So, Aditi, tell us a
little bit about Tache.

00:00:51.703 --> 00:00:54.323
- Sure, so tache means
spot or smudge in French

00:00:54.323 --> 00:00:57.387
because every time I'm wearing
my chef coat or my apron,

00:00:57.387 --> 00:00:59.900
I usually have a smudge of
chocolate on it somewhere.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.336
So hopefully you will leave

00:01:01.336 --> 00:01:03.090
with a smudge of chocolate on you.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.475
Actually, you don't have aprons, so...

00:01:04.475 --> 00:01:05.308
(laughing)

00:01:05.308 --> 00:01:06.971
Hopefully it'll be in your mouth.

00:01:06.971 --> 00:01:09.100
So, I do have a variety of chocolate.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.301
So, white chocolate, not
real chocolate, guys.

00:01:13.301 --> 00:01:14.159
- What?

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:16.421
- Yeah, white chocolate is made up of

00:01:16.421 --> 00:01:18.663
cocoa butter, milk solids, and sugar.

00:01:18.663 --> 00:01:21.248
So, it contains absolutely no cacao.

00:01:21.248 --> 00:01:22.612
- My mind is blown right now.

00:01:22.612 --> 00:01:24.102
So this isn't real chocolate?

00:01:24.102 --> 00:01:25.095
- Let's go up the scale.

00:01:25.095 --> 00:01:27.928
So, let's try some milk chocolate.

00:01:29.065 --> 00:01:29.948
- Loving it.

00:01:29.948 --> 00:01:31.211
- This is what heaven is like.

00:01:31.211 --> 00:01:34.324
- The main differences
between milk and dark,

00:01:34.324 --> 00:01:37.659
milk chocolate contains
a ton more milk in it

00:01:37.659 --> 00:01:41.252
and it also contains some cocoa mass,

00:01:41.252 --> 00:01:44.751
some vanilla to give it
a little bit of flavor,

00:01:44.751 --> 00:01:45.951
and some cocoa butter.

00:01:45.951 --> 00:01:47.907
- It says it's only 35% chocolate,

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.052
so it can only get
better from here, right?

00:01:50.052 --> 00:01:51.136
- Yeah, exactly. It has to.

00:01:51.136 --> 00:01:52.976
- So, the next one that
you guys are trying

00:01:52.976 --> 00:01:55.476
is an 81% dark chocolate.

00:01:56.736 --> 00:01:59.889
I think you'll be able to taste
more of the nuances in it.

00:01:59.889 --> 00:02:00.722
- This is a different level.

00:02:00.722 --> 00:02:03.021
This is sort of like,
there's a bitterness to this.

00:02:03.021 --> 00:02:06.668
- It's just like blowing my
mind to taste pure chocolate.

00:02:06.668 --> 00:02:08.776
- It's like, and we haven't
even reached pure chocolate yet.

00:02:08.776 --> 00:02:10.013
We're at like, 81%.

00:02:10.013 --> 00:02:11.089
- We haven't reached nirvana?

00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:12.344
- No. (laughing)

00:02:12.344 --> 00:02:15.746
- Obviously, 100% chocolate
is 100% chocolate,

00:02:15.746 --> 00:02:17.333
but what does that mean?

00:02:17.333 --> 00:02:20.463
- So, 100% chocolate comes
with no frills attached,

00:02:20.463 --> 00:02:23.252
so it is just an organic chocolate mass.

00:02:23.252 --> 00:02:25.687
Basically, they take cacao beans

00:02:25.687 --> 00:02:28.093
and they ground them up nice and fine,

00:02:28.093 --> 00:02:30.863
and then they form it
into a nice little brick

00:02:30.863 --> 00:02:32.560
that looks like that.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.228
When we get it, we just chip away at it

00:02:35.228 --> 00:02:38.289
and put it into our
double boiler over there

00:02:38.289 --> 00:02:42.539
and melt it and make it
into wonderful concoctions.

00:02:42.539 --> 00:02:43.372
I like that.

00:02:43.372 --> 00:02:44.793
- All right, all right.

00:02:44.793 --> 00:02:46.062
- [Aditi] I think that looks great.

00:02:46.062 --> 00:02:48.479
- Let's get ready for
these silky mouth feels.

00:02:48.479 --> 00:02:49.479
- All right.

00:02:51.007 --> 00:02:52.730
(laughing)

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.807
- Heaven tastes a little
different than I thought.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.410
Your chocolate is definitely bold.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.159
- Whoa, man. Bitter is just it.

00:02:59.159 --> 00:03:01.215
That is like the best
way to describe this.

00:03:01.215 --> 00:03:02.900
- I don't know, kind of
like the taste of tobacco

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:03.900
or like, a cigar.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.314
- So this is like literally day and night.

00:03:05.314 --> 00:03:07.710
I mean, not just based off how it looks,

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.988
but definitely by the way it tastes.

00:03:09.988 --> 00:03:11.099
- This is like a little kid

00:03:11.099 --> 00:03:12.782
when their parents give
them wine and they're like,

00:03:12.782 --> 00:03:15.937
"Oh, I know this is supposed
to taste good, but it doesn't."

00:03:15.937 --> 00:03:18.448
- It's an acquired taste.

00:03:18.448 --> 00:03:20.741
- I guess I was naive in not knowing

00:03:20.741 --> 00:03:22.579
what the taste of chocolate was,

00:03:22.579 --> 00:03:24.977
because the chocolate
we know is mixed with

00:03:24.977 --> 00:03:27.780
vanilla, and cocoa butter, and sugar,

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.284
and all these great things.

00:03:29.284 --> 00:03:31.690
It just shows just how brilliant

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.285
the chocolatiers of the world are.

00:03:33.285 --> 00:03:35.361
Having the more pure
chocolate made me realize

00:03:35.361 --> 00:03:37.489
I'm a basic chocolate
lover, and that's okay.

00:03:37.489 --> 00:03:39.834
- I'm gonna ask you to rest
a little piece of chocolate

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:42.436
in between your tongue
and the roof of your mouth

00:03:42.436 --> 00:03:44.504
and kind of swish it around your pallette

00:03:44.504 --> 00:03:46.215
like you would do with fine wine.

00:03:46.215 --> 00:03:48.387
- [Man] What? We're getting fancy as hell

00:03:48.387 --> 00:03:50.268
in this chocolate factory.

